      "locator": "Source paragraph 061",
      "ordinal": 0,
      "role": "SUPPORTING_CONTEXT",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.newadvent.org/fathers/2915.htm",
      "contentSha256": "154a9fe147537637e6e381d994c55fe4139802741e6040d800c4874094e5a80d",
      "excerpt": "Why, seeing that Lazarus' soul is occupied with his present blessings and turns round to look at nothing that he has left, while the rich man is still attached, with a cement as it were, even after death, to the life of ",
      "editorialStatus": "SOURCE_EXCERPT_REVIEWED_NOT_DOCTRINALLY_CERTIFIED"
    },
    {
      "questionId": "gregory-09",
      "passageId": "passage_68307dccb2e4fbd8a0a5fd937aecfae5",
      "editionId": "edition_7f982e9d2f0acc26526b91f0042dee75",
      "locator": "Source paragraph 086",
      "ordinal": 1,
      "role": "DIRECT_ANSWER",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.newadvent.org/fathers/2915.htm",
      "contentSha256": "e95ed15259ca6bccf2fcbae037e7ab785fa70e0b4387623f9197e6f5acd6c6b6",
      "excerpt": "unexamined, we will expound the truth as to these points as follows. First let us get a clear notion as to the scope of this doctrine; in other words, what is the end that Holy Scripture has in view in promulgating it an",
      "editorialStatus": "SOURCE_EXCERPT_REVIEWED_NOT_DOCTRINALLY_CERTIFIED"
    },
    {
      "questionId": "gregory-09",
